    {
      "rule": "A local timeout fences the owned run until verified shutdown, then canonical same-session resume may recover stranded work; cancellation authority and quarantine remain durable.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/run.mjs",
        "lib/commands/resume.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/task_prepare.mjs"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "the existing timeout caller still uses the shared capability-aware stop path",
        "both immediate stop confirmation and restart reconciliation validate matching local run/process-tree cessation",
        "live descendants, unreadable process state and missing/different current identity do not release the timeout fence",
        "read-only inspection never clears fences or signals processes",
        "only local implementation timeout is recoverable; remote, operator and intake stops remain fenced",
        "a later timeout cannot downgrade a stronger stop, including after confirmation",
        "native verified group shutdown prevents overlap with detached tools",
        "collection and settlement check quarantine before result application or exit inference",
        "current projection and reconciliation preserve the cancelled outcome when raw exit acknowledgement is missing",
        "late successful output/cache cannot overwrite cancelled state or canonical result",
        "legacy timeout metadata repairs without inventing old paid intent",
        "explicit resume preserves provider/session, branch/worktree, partial/carried files, unpushed diagnostics and sandbox settings",
        "one new owned continuation is persisted; previous operation identity remains intact",
        "unknown cost remains null; no model/provider defaults or live availability change",
        "publication, PR writer, review, readiness and human merge boundaries remain canonical"
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "local timeout recovery preserves stranded work and explicitly resumes one owned session after shutdown",
        "local timeout fences survive failed inspection, changed ownership and concurrent operator cancellation",
        "remote and preparation timeout fences remain permanent after authoritative shutdown",
        "released local timeout quarantine preserves cancelled settlement when raw exit evidence is missing",
        "native local timeout waits for detached tools before releasing the same-session continuation fence"
      ]
    }
  ],
